Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: select host requests for non-continuous clocks

Configure request selection before enabling the controller, while its existing
state check and controller mutex protect the operation. The non-continuous
clock path otherwise leaves DSI_LANE_CTRL bit 24 set. Both Neo3 controllers
were observed in that state with corrupted physical output, despite correct
linear framebuffer contents. This does not itself establish a display fix.

Adapted from the diagnosis in PicoFrame patch 0015, commit 79110e2
(https://github.com/TheReal-Flo/PicoFrame). Keep continuous-clock behavior and
controllers without the request-selection callback unchanged.

--- a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_ctrl.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_ctrl.c
@@ -3480,6 +3480,10 @@
-	if (state == DSI_CTRL_ENGINE_ON)
+	if (state == DSI_CTRL_ENGINE_ON) {
+		if (!dsi_ctrl->host_config.common_config.force_hs_clk_lane &&
+				dsi_ctrl->hw.ops.hs_req_sel)
+			dsi_ctrl->hw.ops.hs_req_sel(&dsi_ctrl->hw, true);
 		dsi_ctrl->hw.ops.ctrl_en(&dsi_ctrl->hw, true);
-	else
+	} else {
 		dsi_ctrl->hw.ops.ctrl_en(&dsi_ctrl->hw, false);
+	}
 
 	DSI_CTRL_DEBUG(dsi_ctrl, "Set host engine state = %d\n", state);
